{
 "annotations": {
  "destructiveHint": false,
  "idempotentHint": false,
  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": false
 },
 "description": "Convert raw or loosely formatted screenplay text (Chinese, English, or mixed \u2014 including Japanese broadcast-drama format and Chinese colon-style dialogue scripts) into professionally structured screenplay blocks and a print-ready PDF on a fixed typewriter character grid identical to narracore.cn. Use it for screenplay formatting, import, or producing a shareable screenplay PDF \u2014 NOT for general prose rewriting or story editing.\n\nINPUT (contract_version 3) \u2014 two modes:\n\u2022 input_format=\"text\" (default): line-based screenplay text, one element per line \u2014 scene headings (\"INT. LAB - DAY\", \"\u7b2c N \u573a \u2026\"), CHARACTER names in CAPS or CJK on their own line, short dialogue lines after them, standalone (\u2026) parentheticals, standalone transitions (\"CUT TO:\", \"\u5207\u81f3\uff1a\u2026\"). Inline dialogue \u540d\u524d\u300c\u30bb\u30ea\u30d5\u300d and \u4eba\u540d\uff1a\u53f0\u8bcd is parsed natively. An unbroken wall of text renders as continuous action and is flagged UNRESOLVED_STRUCTURE.\n\u2022 input_format=\"blocks\": typed blocks validated and rendered EXACTLY as submitted, never re-classified; ids echoed. CHAINING: to run other tools on this screenplay, pass back the BLOCKS you received \u2014 not the plain text (it parses differently). The same screenplay is charged once per 24h across analyze/diagnose/convert/video-prompt tools; check_video_prompts is free.\n\u2022 output=\"validate_only\": structure check + diagnostics only, free.\n\nBefore delivering: read diagnostics[] (code/severity/line or block_id/message/suggested_action) with the user; confidence = share of non-ambiguous lines, NOT accuracy.\n\nBilling: one credit = one screenplay for 24h across the screenplay tools (or one film analysis / one story project). Free tier: one credit per day per visitor, no key. Failed calls are never charged; the same request_id never double-charges. On free_tier_exhausted or quota_exhausted: relay the price and purchase link from the response verbatim; never invent a license key.\n\nFull parameter manual (cover/header/footer, examples): https://narracore.app/llms.txt",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "properties": {
   "blocks": {
    "description": "Typed blocks (required when input_format=\"blocks\")",
    "items": {
     "properties": {
      "delivery": {
       "description": "dialogue: delivery hint, rendered as a parenthetical before the line",
       "maxLength": 120,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "id": {
       "description": "Your id for this block; echoed in output",
       "maxLength": 64,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "location": {
       "maxLength": 120,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "scene_number": {
       "maxLength": 16,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "speaker": {
       "description": "dialogue: speaker name; a character line is derived when rendering",
       "maxLength": 64,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "text": {
       "description": "Block text (scene_heading may omit it if location/time_of_day given)",
       "maxLength": 200000,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "time_of_day": {
       "maxLength": 16,
       "type": "string"
      },
      "type": {
       "enum": [
        "scene_heading",
        "action",
        "character",
        "parenthetical",
        "dialogue",
        "transition",
        "shot",
        "note"
       ],
       "type": "string"
      }
     },
     "required": [
      "type"
     ],
     "type": "object"
    },
    "maxItems": 2000,
    "type": "array"
   },
   "content_language": {
    "description": "Content language (default: auto-detect)",
    "enum": [
     "zh",
     "en",
     "auto"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "cover": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "Cover page fields \u2014 any field present adds a cover page (not counted in page numbers); date defaults to today (UTC) when omitted",
    "properties": {
     "author": {
      "maxLength": 2000,
      "type": "string"
     },
     "date": {
      "maxLength": 64,
      "type": "string"
     },
     "title": {
      "maxLength": 2000,
      "type": "string"
     },
     "version": {
      "maxLength": 64,
      "type": "string"
     }
    },
    "type": "object"
   },
   "footer": {
    "description": "Explicit footer (centered below the text box); same value resolution as header",
    "properties": {
     "items": {
      "items": {
       "enum": [
        "title",
        "author",
        "date",
        "version",
        "page_number"
       ],
       "type": "string"
      },
      "maxItems": 5,
      "minItems": 1,
      "type": "array"
     }
    },
    "required": [
     "items"
    ],
    "type": "object"
   },
   "header": {
    "description": "Explicit running header (overrides the default page-number line): field values come from cover; missing fields are skipped; page_number renders N/M at the right edge",
    "properties": {
     "items": {
      "items": {
       "enum": [
        "title",
        "author",
        "date",
        "version",
        "page_number"
       ],
       "type": "string"
      },
      "maxItems": 5,
      "minItems": 1,
      "type": "array"
     }
    },
    "required": [
     "items"
    ],
    "type": "object"
   },
   "include": {
    "description": "Receipt body shape (default both): blocks=typed blocks only, plain_text=formatted text only \u2014 halves the receipt for large screenplays; validate_only always echoes blocks",
    "enum": [
     "blocks",
     "plain_text",
     "both"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "input_format": {
    "description": "text (default): line-based screenplay text parsed server-side. blocks: submit typed blocks directly \u2014 validated and rendered as-is, never re-classified.",
    "enum": [
     "text",
     "blocks"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "license_key": {
    "description": "License key NRC-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX (optional \u2014 free daily quota works without one)",
    "pattern": "^NRC-[A-Z2-9]{4}(-[A-Z2-9]{4}){3}$",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "output": {
    "description": "pdf_and_blocks (default) / blocks_only / validate_only (free structure check, no render)",
    "enum": [
     "pdf_and_blocks",
     "blocks_only",
     "validate_only"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "request_id": {
    "description": "Idempotency key (optional)",
    "maxLength": 64,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "text": {
    "description": "Raw screenplay text, one element per line (required when input_format=\"text\")",
    "maxLength": 200000,
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
